1	// pattern: Imperative Shell
2	//
3	// The auth.md agent claim ceremony (spec Step 4). Two endpoints, split by audience:
4	//
5	//   - `POST /agent/identity/claim` — the *agent* starts (or resumes) a ceremony for a registration
6	//     it holds a `claim_token` for. Public: the `claim_token` is the agent's credential, so no user
7	//     session is required here. Mainly serves the `anonymous` flow, whose registration returned only
8	//     a `claim_token` and no `user_code`; `service_auth` / first-seen `identity_assertion` already
9	//     minted a `user_code` at registration, so re-initiating idempotently re-emits the pending one.
10	//   - `POST /agent/identity/claim/confirm` — the *account owner* (full-access session/OAuth token)
11	//     submits the `user_code` the agent showed them. This binds the registration to their DID (for
12	//     an ownerless `anonymous` identity), mints the post-claim `identity_assertion`, and flips the
13	//     identity `active → claimed` so its assertion can be exchanged at the token endpoint. This is
14	//     the wallet-facing surface (Obsign's claim-approval screen).
15	//
16	// Registration lives in `agent_identity.rs`; the assertion-minting / claim-block / error helpers are
17	// shared via `auth::agent_assertion` (routes may not import from one another).
18	
